{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the Levite who is in your gates.</b> The meaning concerns the house of Levi, that you accept their wages — do not abandon him; rather give him according to the gift of your hand. And the closer interpretation is that it speaks of the first tithe, because he mentioned the second tithe; he said, do not think that you discharge your obligation with the second tithe alone." "And the meaning of <b>who is in your gates:</b> for to him who is in his gate he shall give the first tithe, and he may not say, \"Let him be with me and I will take it to another Levite,\" or \"I have already given it.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:27.268220174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}